"The failure is a pandas type-coercion detail: the first row's `wm_before` of `None` was upcast to `NaT`, and `NaT` isn't caught by an `is None` test. Let me fix the formatter to handle both.\n\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ calls>\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ invoke name=\"python\">\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter name=\"query\" string=\"true\"># --- fix: NaT-aware formatter (first row has no prior watermark) ---\ndef h(t):\n    return \"—(first)\" if t is None or pd.isna(t) else t.strftime(\"%H:%M:%S\")\n\nshow = ev.assign(\n    event_time=ev.event_time.dt.strftime(\"%H:%M:%S\"),\n    wm_before=ev.wm_before.map(h),\n    wm_after=ev.wm_after.map(h),\n    max_et=ev.max_et.dt.strftime(\"%H:%M:%S\"),\n    window=ev.window.dt.strftime(\"%H:%M\"),\n    win_fire_arr=ev.win_fire_arr.map(lambda a: \"end-of-input\" if pd.isna(a) else f\"arr {int(a)}\"),\n)[[\"arrival\",\"event_id\",\"product_id\",\"event_time\",\"max_et\",\"wm_before\",\"wm_after\",\n   \"status\",\"late_by_s\",\"window\",\"win_fire_arr\",\"late_for_closed_window\"]]\nprint(show.to_string(index=False))\n\nprint(f\"\\nfinal watermark      : {h(ev.wm_after.iloc[-1])}  \"\n      f\"(max event_time {h(ev.max_et.iloc[-1])} - 30s)\")\nprint(f\"final WM bound       : events with event_time >= 00:09:10 are still on-time\")\nprint(f\"on-time / late       : {(ev.status=='on-time').sum()} / {(ev.status=='LATE').sum()}\")\nprint(f\"late vs closed window: {ev.late_for_closed_window.sum()} of {len(ev)}\")\n</｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter>\n</｜｜DSML｜｜ invoke>\n</｜｜DSML｜｜ calls>"